---
description: Testing, linting, and commit conventions
globs: ["**/*.spec.ts", "**/*.e2e-spec.ts"]
alwaysApply: false
---

- Every new service method that contains business logic gets a unit test with mocked Prisma/repository dependencies (use Nest's `Test.createTestingModule`)
- Auth, MFA, and RBAC logic require test coverage for both success and failure/edge paths (expired token, reused token, wrong tenant, insufficient permission) — not just the happy path
- E2E tests (`test:e2e`) cover full request flows for auth (register → login → refresh → logout) and any new critical flow
- Run `pnpm lint` and `pnpm format` before considering a change complete; don't disable ESLint rules inline without justification
- Use Commitizen conventional commits (`pnpm commit`) — don't hand-write non-conventional commit messages for anything touching shared history
- Never commit `.env`, real secrets, or test fixtures containing real tokens/credentials